Runs for building and testing on Lean v4.35.0 as well as v4.34.1 (branch compat), 2026-10-29, on the
build host, on the code of caebbb5 (the rename of `given`; its merge with main's batchrun change,
cf888e3, touches only scripts/remote.sh).  The runs were made on an earlier copy of that commit whose
tree differed only in a comment of scripts/remote.sh.  v4.35.0 from another elan volume on the host
that holds the release (its commit in toolchain.txt), in ~/lean-http-compat; v4.34.1 from
b8perf-elan, in ~/lean-http-compat-434; both in localhost/b8perf-lean, uv's CPython 3.14.8 for the
servers.  The two ran side by side; the host was shared and saturated (load average about 290 to
340 on 128 CPUs).

The first v4.35.0 build failed in LeanHttp/Call/Redirect.lean: v4.35.0 parses `given`, `requires` and
`ensures` as clauses of a def contract and refuses them as names in a def's signature (its
Lean/Parser/Command.lean, `optDeclSig`).  Renaming the identifier `given` to `firstCredentials` was the
only change needed.  v4.35.0/first-build.txt is that build's output (the last 80 lines of
lake build).

$ LEAN_HTTP_ELAN=<volume> bash logs/2026-10-29/compat/run.sh v4.35.0     (from the laptop; the script says what it runs)
$ bash logs/2026-10-29/compat/run.sh v4.34.1
$ rsync --archive buildhost:lean-http-compat/out/compat/ logs/2026-10-29/compat/v4.35.0/
$ rsync --archive buildhost:lean-http-compat-434/out/compat/ logs/2026-10-29/compat/v4.34.1/

<toolchain>/toolchain.txt   lean --version inside the container.
<toolchain>/suites/   run-suites.sh (here, as logs/2026-10-29/wire/ had it), from a build with
              .lake/build removed first: build and build-tests (no warnings); the axioms of the
              exchange, codec, pool and planner theorems (on propext, Classical.choice and
              Quot.sound at most, no sorryAx); unit (119 checks), codec, response-codec, traces,
              props, explore, codec-diff with its control, the pool's suites and the planner's
              call-tests and call-diff.  Every file ends with exit status 0, on both toolchains.
<toolchain>/net/      $ CTR_EXTRA='--sysctl net.ipv4.tcp_syn_retries=2' scripts/remote.sh bash tests/net/run.sh
              v4.35.0: 291 passed, 0 failed, 1 known limitation (dns-timeout's exit, as in NOTES.md).
              v4.34.1: 289 passed, 2 failed, 1 known limitation.  The failures: retry-503-backoff
              (a retry woke more than 30 ms after its delay: gaps 45 and 85 ms for delays 23 and 49)
              and stream-drain (the rest of a body not drained within the 100 ms drain limit, so
              the connection was not reused).
<toolchain>/net-rerun/   The two groups those checks belong to, five times each on each toolchain:
              $ scripts/remote.sh bash tests/net/run.sh retry-after stream-abandon
              stream-drain passed all ten runs.  retry-503-backoff failed in 2 of 5 runs on each
              toolchain, each time a retry woke 34 to 100 ms past its delay, so it is the check's
              30 ms tolerance on a saturated host, not the toolchain: the code under test is the
              same on both, and the full v4.35.0 run passed it.
